larmorx-gpl holds bit-exact replicas of neuroimaging tools of the GPL licence family: Rust
translations of their source code, written to give their output bit for bit. Today it holds one,
tedana's t2smap. The larmorx-gpl program (crates larmorx-gpl-cli and larmorx-gpl-tedana) is
distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only (see LICENSE). It comes with
ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY. Each translated file names its licence in an SPDX header and its origin in
a comment; each crate's PROVENANCE.md lists the upstream files it was translated from and the
changes made.

The program is a separate work from larmorx (Apache-2.0), which runs it as a separate process
when it is installed and exchanges files with it only. It does not present itself as tedana or
as any other upstream tool, and it is not endorsed by tedana's developers.

Source code. The source of this directory (the tedana translation and the program) is in every
larmorx-gpl wheel (its licence files). The program's complete Corresponding Source, with the
larmorx crates it is built with (crates/ of the repository) and the Rust crates its Cargo.lock
pins, is published at https://github.com/karellopez/larmorx (directory crates-gpl/, at the
commit of each release; the release's tag names it).


Translated works
================

tedana 26.0.3 (TE-Dependent ANAlysis of multi-echo fMRI), Copyright 2023, The ME-ICA Developers
(https://github.com/ME-ICA/tedana) - GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
  Translated: the t2smap workflow and command line (tedana/workflows/t2smap.py, parser_utils.py)
  and the parts of tedana/decay.py, combine.py, utils.py, io.py and
  resources/config/outputs.json it uses (crate larmorx-gpl-tedana; PROVENANCE.md lists them).
  Its licence text, as tedana ships it, is LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-tedana.txt. tedana names version
  2.1 of the LGPL and no later version, and none of its files carries another notice.
  Modified: translated from Python to Rust in 2026 by Karel Lopez Vilaret; the defects of
  tedana's that change results are corrected by default and reproduced on request
  (LARMORX_UPSTREAM_DEFECTS=reproduce; the TED entries of the repository's
  docs/findings/upstream-defects.md); the maths default to correctly rounded functions.
  Section 3 of the LGPL version 2.1 permits applying the terms of the ordinary GNU General
  Public License to a copy of the library instead, naming a version newer than 2: this
  translation is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only, so that it
  can include the Apache-2.0 larmorx crates it is built with. The change is irreversible for
  this copy (section 3).


